gold: anchor the divergence with CE, log the entropy that collapses, and let the
guard warn without stopping

Applies to: github.com/laminair/gb-steps-distillation at a5d59bc4 -- the commit this
            step's code_config pins -- under a DIFFERENT directory than the one the
            hunks name. Remap gold/ onto src/gb_steps_post_training/distillation/:

              cd <checkout>/src/gb_steps_post_training/distillation
              patch -p2 -F3 < ce_anchor_and_entropy_guard.diff

            or, equivalently, from the checkout root:

              git apply -p2 --directory=src/gb_steps_post_training/distillation -C1 \
                steps/distill/distill-gold/skypilot/patches/ce_anchor_and_entropy_guard.diff

            ALL SIX HUNKS APPLY, but two need fuzz 2 and the offsets run to 1,137
            lines, because the public repo's trainer has moved a long way from the
            kd-sandbox commit the diff was cut against. Fuzz can place a hunk
            somewhere plausible and wrong, so placement was verified per function
            rather than taken from patch's exit code (2026-09-28): the six fields
            land in CustomGOLDConfig, the CE term in compute_loss, the new
            _maybe_act_on_entropy_collapse beside it, and the logging in log(). Every
            dependency resolves -- cross_entropy_loss is a pre-existing @staticmethod,
            and shifted_student_logits/_teacher_logits/_labels are assigned about 75
            lines above the CE term. Re-verify the same way after any pin bump.

            It does NOT carry min_completion_length: that key needs a trainer field
